Z||000000||Richard Parnell||08-04-2000||03:01 PM||||While I'm waiting for parts for my engine swap, I've been fooling with the 5 speed Isuzu tranny which is still in the car with the 4 banger.  The clutch will not disengage and I'm pretty sure at this point that there is something wrong on the inside eg. bad throwout bearing or fork bent.  While trying for one last time to bleed the hydraulics, I noticed that the clutch pedal does not go all the way to the floor as I've heard others say theirs' does. It hits a metal crossbar before it gets down to the carpet.  Could there be something out of adjustment down there?  I did install a new steel pedal.. All this is academic as I am also going to pick up another 5 speed and have it checked out before sticking the 350 in.  I'm just curious now and am killing time before the main overhaul.  Still I don't remembeer hearing that metal click (when the pedal hits that crossbar) previously.  Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-04-2000||03:24 PM||||Just outta curiosity, does the clutch temorarily work after bleeding it?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||08-04-2000||03:41 PM||||No||||reg||9
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||08-04-2000||07:14 PM||||It's either worked and stayed good for a year or so or didn't work.  It's never worked for a little while then faded. I still keep thinking about a cable setup for the clutch pedal.  But the geometry is beyound me.||||reg||8
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||10:59 AM||||Richard,<BR>What year is your Fiero? I take it that you replaced the aluminum pedal for a steelone. Look under the dash for an obstruction in your pedal travel. It sounds like the pedal is binding on something preventing it 's full travel.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||08-07-2000||02:48 PM||||Yes, it hits a metal crossbar on the downward swing.  The cross bar goes across the main supports and stops the pedal just above the carpet. It looks aluminum, no corrosion. I can't see any way to adjust it further towards the floor.  The pedal I replaced was also steel.  I only replaced it out of desperation.  When I compared it to the new pedal it was exactly the same.  So I assume it was not bent.  So I have an extra steel pedal if some one's interested.  Although the cost of shipping from Hawaii may make it not worth the effort.||||reg||1
